	<entry>
		<title type="html"><![CDATA[Réponse à&#160;:  [RESOLU] [PAF v2.2.0] instance "pgsqld" is not listening]]></title>
		<link rel="alternate" href="http://forums.postgresql.fr/viewtopic.php?pid=26123#p26123"/>
		<content type="html"><![CDATA[<p>Voilà ça marche :-)</p><p>Pour ceux qui rencontreraient le même problème, il ne faut pas oublier d&#039;ajouter pgport dans l&#039;ordre de création de la resource quand vous n&#039;utulisez pas le port par défaut (5432).<br />Exemple :</p><div class="quotebox"><blockquote><div><p>pcs -f clusterCRM.xml resource create pgsqld ocf:heartbeat:pgsqlms \<br />&#160; &#160; bindir=/logiciels/postgres/product/9.3/bin pgport=5433 pgdata=/xxx/admin&#160; &#160; &#160;\<br />&#160; &#160; op start timeout=60s&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160;\<br />&#160; &#160; op stop timeout=60s&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; \<br />&#160; &#160; op promote timeout=30s&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160;\<br />&#160; &#160; op demote timeout=120s&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160;\<br />&#160; &#160; op monitor interval=15s timeout=10s role=&quot;Master&quot;&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; \<br />&#160; &#160; op monitor interval=16s timeout=10s role=&quot;Slave&quot;&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160;\<br />&#160; &#160; op notify timeout=60s&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; \</p></div></blockquote></div><p>Merci Jehan-Guillaume pour l&#039;oeil avisé.</p>]]></content>
